    "body": "agent a2df480aac767f044 · patch staged in worktree-agent-a2df480aac767f044 (uncommitted, awaiting main's review/commit).\nCause: lead_fit::plan_leads accepts a lead within slack (5 um) of the legal region; a straight lead tangent to a round ring leaves it at once (L^2/2R), so the shrunk 0.25 mm linear lead's start sat ~4.5 um outside the eroded disc. No at-depth link to a point outside the certified room can be proved -> named second dive.\nFix: new lead_fit::seat_inside - a straight lead-in whose start is truly past the boundary (> 1e-6 mm; a start ON a straight wall is untouched, keeping vertical_arc_entry's axis-aligned G18 lead) is stepped in along the air normal until it is on the legal side and at least the chord tolerance clear of the boundary (clear of the ring's flattened chords, which the verifier's Crossing law reads); segs_hold rechecked; else unchanged.\nTests: one_descent now pins exactly one descent per level for all 36 bore configs incl. linear, no 'second dive' note anywhere; the old owed test becomes the_linear_lead_bore_lands_its_one_descent_on_the_lead_start (no second dive; non-centre-cutting tool never plunges). Green: motion one_descent/machining2d/entry_approach/center_cut_law, gate -Tier quick, app golden_cl (no golden moved)/lead_approach/vertical_arc_entry, clippy -p camcraft-motion -D warnings.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
